# Build context filter for `docker build` (ADR-013). Without this, every image
# build ships the whole repo (incl. node_modules) to the daemon and `COPY . .`
# bakes it into the layer.
#
# NOTE — `foundation/` is deliberately NOT excluded. It is a git submodule whose
# packages are workspace members (`pnpm-workspace.yaml`); the build needs its
# real contents. Ensure it is checked out (`git submodule update --init`) before
# building — an empty foundation/ fails the install with unresolved @arad/*.

# --- Node.js / pnpm ---------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm-debug.log
npm-debug.log*

# --- Build outputs (regenerated in the container) ---------------------------
**/dist/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
**/.cache/
**/build/
**/coverage/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- VCS + meta -------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitmodules

# --- Secrets — never in an image layer (deploy/scripts/secret-grep.sh) ------
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --- Editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.cursor/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Docs + dev-only deploy artefacts ---------------------------------------
docs/
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CLAUDE.md
LICENSE
*.md
!apps/**/README.md
!packages/**/README.md
deploy/dev/

# --- Test / CI noise --------------------------------------------------------
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.db.test.ts
**/__tests__/
**/__snapshots__/
**/vitest.config.*
.biomecache
